 "C0": {
  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract; Section 1; Section 2",
  "quote": "we ask if we can design a selection algorithm that satisfies fairness",
  "note": "The paper studies random selection algorithms (sortition) over an exogenous metric space over the population. There is no aggregation of agents' submitted inputs into a collective decision: no ballots, votes or reports are submitted; the algorithm's input is a pairwise distance metric fixed by the model, and the agents take no action. It is closer to clustering/fair-selection than to a voting rule."
